IDCAMS REPRO copies data from one VSAM dataset to another. Here's a complete working example:

//REPROCOPY JOB (ACCT),CLASS=A,MSGCLASS=X
//STEP1    EXEC PGM=IDCAMS
//SYSPRINT DD  SYSOUT=*
//SYSIN    DD  *
  REPRO -
    INFILE(INDD) -
    OUTFILE(OUTDD) -
    REUSE
/*
//INDD     DD  DSN=OLD.VSAM.CLUSTER,DISP=SHR
//OUTDD    DD  DSN=NEW.VSAM.CLUSTER,
//             DISP=(NEW,CATLG,DELETE),
//             SPACE=(TRK,(100,50))

Key parameters:
- INFILE: Source dataset (must exist)
- OUTFILE: Target dataset (pre-allocate space)
- REUSE: Allows re-copying to existing dataset
- Use SHR for input, NEW for output
- Both datasets must be VSAM KSDS or RRDS
- Target cluster must exist or be created via DEFINE

Common options:
- NUMREC=n: Copy only first n records
- SKIP=n: Skip first n records
- FROMKEY/TOKEY: Copy key range for KSDS
- FROMADDR/TOADDR: Copy address range for RRDS

IDCAMS LISTCAT displays comprehensive information about VSAM catalogs and cluster definitions. Here's how to use it:

//LISTCAT JOB (ACCT),CLASS=A,MSGCLASS=X
//STEP1   EXEC PGM=IDCAMS
//SYSPRINT DD  SYSOUT=*
//SYSIN    DD  *
  LISTCAT CATALOG(MASTER.CATALOG) -
    ENTRY(MYAPP.VSAM.CLUSTER) -
    ALL
/*

For KSDS cluster and related components:
//STEP2   EXEC PGM=IDCAMS
//SYSPRINT DD  SYSOUT=*
//SYSIN    DD  *
  LISTCAT ENTRY(SALES.KSDS) ALL
/*

For all catalogs:
//STEP3   EXEC PGM=IDCAMS
//SYSPRINT DD  SYSOUT=*
//SYSIN    DD  *
  LISTCAT CATALOG
/*

Output includes:
- Cluster attributes: IMBED, REPLICATE, FREESPACE, RECORDS
- Data component: KEYLEN, KEYOFF, RECORDSIZE, AVGLRECL
- Index component: LEVELS, SEQUENCE SET RBA, CONTROL AREA SIZE
- Allocation: PRIMARY, SECONDARY, ALLOCATED, USED space
- Recovery info: OWNERSHIP, EXPIRATION DATE, CREATION DATE
- Replication status and device type

Common options:
- ALL: Complete listing with all details
- LEVEL(x): Show x-level entries and their dependents
- ENTRIES: Show just entry names without details

IDCAMS ALTER modifies attributes of existing VSAM clusters. Here's a comprehensive example:

//ALTERCLUST JOB (ACCT),CLASS=A,MSGCLASS=X
//STEP1      EXEC PGM=IDCAMS
//SYSPRINT   DD  SYSOUT=*
//SYSIN      DD  *
  ALTER MYAPP.VSAM.KSDS -
    FREESPACE(20 10) -
    OWNER(NEWOWNER) -
    PASSWORDS(WRITE PASSWORD123 -
              READ  PASSWORD456) -
    SHAREOPTIONS(2 3)
/*

To enable replication:
//STEP2      EXEC PGM=IDCAMS
//SYSPRINT   DD  SYSOUT=*
//SYSIN      DD  *
  ALTER SALES.KSDS -
    REPLICATE -
    DATACLASS(REPLICAT)
/*

To change IMBED status:
//STEP3      EXEC PGM=IDCAMS
//SYSPRINT   DD  SYSOUT=*
//SYSIN      DD  *
  ALTER INVENTORY.VSAM -
    IMBED -
    NOIMBED
/*

Key modifiable attributes:
- FREESPACE(CA% CI%): Primary % and Control Interval %
- OWNER: New owner name (max 8 characters)
- PASSWORDS: Master, Alter, Read, Write passwords
- SHAREOPTIONS(X Y): X=cross-region, Y=cross-system
- REPLICATE/NOREPL: Enable/disable replication
- RECATALOG: Update VVDS

Attributes that CANNOT be altered:
- KEYLEN, KEYOFF, RECORDSIZE
- Cluster name, component names
- KSDS/RRDS/ESDS type

Note: FREESPACE changes affect new records only, existing structure unchanged

IDCAMS VERIFY checks VSAM dataset integrity and repairs structural damage. Here's a complete guide:

//VERIFYCLUST JOB (ACCT),CLASS=A,MSGCLASS=X
//STEP1       EXEC PGM=IDCAMS
//SYSPRINT    DD  SYSOUT=*
//SYSIN       DD  *
  VERIFY DATASET(MYAPP.VSAM.KSDS) -
    EXTERNAL
/*

For repairing index damage:
//STEP2       EXEC PGM=IDCAMS
//SYSPRINT    DD  SYSOUT=*
//SYSIN       DD  *
  VERIFY DATASET(SALES.KSDS) -
    CATALOG(MASTER.CATALOG) -
    REPAIR
/*

Verify with REBUILD for severe corruption:
//STEP3       EXEC PGM=IDCAMS
//SYSPRINT    DD  SYSOUT=*
//SYSIN       DD  *
  VERIFY DATASET(INVENTORY.KSDS) -
    EXTERNAL -
    RECOVERY
/*

When to use VERIFY:
- Dataset shows access errors or ABENDs
- Index appears corrupted (wrong key ordering)
- Abnormal job termination while updating cluster
- After hardware failure or catalog problems
- Periodic maintenance on critical VSAM files

What VERIFY does:
- EXTERNAL: Checks data and index components on disk
- Validates Control Area (CA) and Control Interval (CI) integrity
- Verifies key sequencing in index
- Checks space maps and record descriptors
- REPAIR: Rebuilds CA/CI free space information
- RECOVERY: Rebuilds index if severely damaged

Return codes:
- 0: No errors detected
- 8: Minor errors detected, repaired
- 12: Errors requiring REPAIR option
- 16: Severe damage, dataset unusable

Caution: VERIFY locks the dataset; run during maintenance windows
